  "events": [],
  "notes": [
    "the log has no barometer, so the record's altitude track is empty: an RTx's file holds GPS fixes only, and every field is a channel",
    "the log's clock is the GPS's time of day, UTC, `UTC`, in whole seconds. Its zero is the first record's, 17:59:50. The file states no date",
    "times go back 1 times from one record to the next, by up to 1 s. 2 records repeat a time already written. Every record is kept, in the file's order",
    "1 records hold a time that isn't a time of day, such as 4278370088: their times are gaps",
    "`Alt` read in feet, from the `.rtx` files beside the sample exports. The values are whole feet, the `.rtx`'s meters × 3.280 84 rounded down, read as 0.3048 m each",
    "`Vel` and `SOG` kept as written, in units no document states. `SOG` runs about 3.6 times the speed between fixes, as kilometers an hour would. The velocity runs far more than the climb rate while it climbs",
    "`COG` read in degrees, from the positions. It is the course over ground, within a few degrees of the bearing between the fixes either side while the tracker moves",
    "the software writes every record of its `.rtx` file but the last: the `.rtx` holds one more fix"
  ]
